  <h2>Masterclass: Fixing Gimbal Motor Vibration and Micro-Jitters</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><b>Execute Motor Auto-Tuning:</b> Place your fully balanced gimbal onto a stable, vibration-free table surface and trigger an <b>Auto-Tune calibration sequence</b> through your system touchscreen or companion mobile app. This diagnostic protocol assesses your exact camera payload distribution and calibrates optimal PID motor stiffness voltages to prevent high-frequency mechanical hum.</li>
    <li><b>Enforce Strict Mechanical Balancing Sequences:</b> Never force gimbal motors to compensate for clumsy physical balancing. Always manually balance your axes in strict mechanical succession: <i>Tilt Axis (Vertical Pointing) ➔ Tilt Axis (Horizontal Leveling) ➔ Roll Axis (Lateral Balance) ➔ Pan Axis (Base Rotational Center of Gravity)</i>.</li>
  </ol>

